<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aufĭdus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αὔφιδος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in Apulia</i>,
				<i>remarkable for its swift and violent
			course</i>, now <i>Ofanto</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longe sonans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 9, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">violens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 30, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					S. 1, 1, 58</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">on account of its divided outlet: tauriformis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					C. 4, 14, 25</span></i>
			; cf. Mann. Ital. II. p. 30 sq.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aufĭ-dus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Aufidus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stagna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					10, 171</span></i>
			.</div>
